Given an array of 32-bit signed integers, produce an output array of the same length where each position contains the maximum value seen in the input up to and including that position. The input may be empty; in that case, return an empty array. For every index i with 0 <= i < n (where n is the input length), the output at i must equal the mathematical maximum of the first i+1 elements of the input. The mathematical maximum over a sequence is defined recursively on finite sequences, and for the empty sequence it is defined as the minimum 32-bit signed integer (this definition is used internally to characterize prefix maxima but does not affect the empty input case). No assumptions are made about the ordering or distinctness of input values.
spec fn seq_max(a: Seq<i32>) -> i32
fn rolling_max(numbers: Vec<i32>) -> (result: Vec<i32>)

