Given an array of 32-bit unsigned integers, determine whether the array contains at least one even number. Return true if and only if there exists an index k such that 0 ≤ k < length of the array and the element at position k is even. The input may be empty; in that case, return false. During any linear scan of the array to find such an element, it must be preserved that all already-inspected positions contain odd values until an even value is found.
spec fn is_even(n: u32) -> bool
fn is_product_even(arr: &Vec<u32>) -> (result: bool)

