description:
Implement a function that determines whether a given unsigned 64-bit integer is non-prime (composite). Assume the input integer is at least 2. The function must return true if and only if there exists an integer in the range from 2 up to, but not including, the input value that divides the input evenly. Formally, the result must be equivalent to the existence of some integer k with 2 ≤ k < n such that n % k == 0. If the implementation uses iteration to search for a divisor, it must maintain a loop invariant stating that all previously tested integers in the candidate range do not divide the input. The loop must be shown to terminate via a strictly decreasing measure tied to the remaining distance between the current candidate and the input value.
spec fn is_divisible(n: int, divisor: int) -> bool
fn is_non_prime(n: u64) -> (result: bool)

